{"title":"Celsius","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>Celsius</b> (also <b>Centigrade</b>) scale is a system for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Measure\" title=\"Measure\">measuring</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Temperature\" title=\"Temperature\">temperature</a>. Originally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/3/1d3140f515bfc85171266b911c509cdfb47ccb48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> was defined as the temperature at which water freezes at 1 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Atm\" title=\"Atm\">atm</a>, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b966a08f4a3f2b347e0a5212a423d2c2abeba9f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> as the temperature at which water boils at 1 atm.\n</p><p>However, since different thermometers register slightly different temperatures at these points, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Absolute_zero\" title=\"Absolute zero\">absolute zero</a> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triple_point\" title=\"Triple point\">triple point</a> of water are used to fix the Celsius scale. They are defined, respectively, to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/499163872f186fce518a0cdaa5184f4053b63289.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-273.15^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e7bf776c6c12ee2d94ce0dc95568a4938c3e2b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.01^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Conversion\">Conversion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Celsius&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Conversion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Celsius to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fahrenheit\" title=\"Fahrenheit\">Fahrenheit</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be4a19e2136f88874cd8f2f6eadb593579a0602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$^\\circ\\mathrm{F}=\\tfrac{9}{5}{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}+32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" /></li>\n<li>Celsius to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Kelvin\" title=\"Kelvin\">Kelvin</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/480765d64a5ca7968e50aaeafadcb87f9022fd73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{K}={}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}-273.15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"131\" height=\"13\" /></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Celsius&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017122706\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 40/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 262/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1155/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.954      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.954      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6987:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017122706 and revision id 236379. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}